  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Calenduloside C and VMRC-LCP through a series of molecular interactions. Calenduloside C is implicated in targeting Tankyrase-2, which is a target of Tubotaiwine and Cocosamide B, both of which also target VMRC-LCP. This indicates a possible pathway where Calenduloside C may influence VMRC-LCP via Tankyrase-2, potentially through the action of Tubotaiwine or Cocosamide B. Additionally, Calenduloside C is also linked to SF-188, which is a target of (7S,11S)-(+)-12-acetoxysydonic acid, which in turn targets VMRC-LCP. These findings suggest that Calenduloside C may exert its effects on VMRC-LCP through multiple downstream pathways, possibly through the activation or inhibition of key enzymes or proteins involved in the regulation of VMRC-LCP. The scores from the different paths are consistent, indicating a plausible and robust relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
